Subject: fix(action): skip local sandbox host setup when a gateway is configured

The agent action turns the runner into a sandbox host in four steps: install
Podman, configure it rootless, write a local OpenShell gateway config, and
install the OpenShell CLI. That is right for a GitHub-hosted runner, which is a
fresh virtual machine with none of it.

It is wrong for a runner pointed at an OpenShell gateway that already runs
somewhere else. Sandboxes are created on the gateway, so the runner needs no
container runtime, and a gateway config written on the runner never reaches the
gateway it is meant to configure. Fullsend already supports this arrangement:
internal/sandbox/gateway_endpoint.go honours an explicit
OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT and connects directly to a running gateway.

Today those steps run unconditionally and fail on any runner that is not a
virtual machine, because "sudo usermod" and "systemctl --user" are not
available in a container.

Guard the two Podman steps and the local gateway configuration on the absence
of an explicit gateway endpoint, so a runner that hosts its own sandboxes is
unchanged and a runner that does not stops building a second copy of a service
it already has.

Two smaller guards travel with it, for the same reason: skip the OpenShell CLI
installer when the CLI is already on PATH, since the installer needs sudo and a
CDN to reinstall what the image ships; and skip the jsonschema install when it
already imports, since pip refuses an externally managed environment.

Breadboard note: applied to the Fullsend mirror the emulator serves, because it
changes files a workflow reads at run time. Written to be sent upstream as-is.
Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a human-authored change.

diff --git a/action.yml b/action.yml
index 9ed38708..e31382af 100644
--- a/action.yml
+++ b/action.yml
@@ -365,11 +365,27 @@ runs:
 
     - name: Install Podman
       shell: bash
-      run: "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/.github/scripts/install-podman.sh"
+      run: |
+        set -euo pipefail
+        # A runner pointed at an already-running OpenShell gateway does not
+        # host sandboxes itself, so it needs no container runtime. Installing
+        # one would be building a second, local copy of a capability the
+        # environment already provides. See internal/sandbox/gateway_endpoint.go,
+        # which documents connecting directly to an external gateway.
+        if [[ -n "${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT:-}" ]]; then
+          echo "Sandboxes run on the gateway at ${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT}; skipping local Podman."
+          exit 0
+        fi
+        "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/.github/scripts/install-podman.sh"
 
     - name: Configure rootless Podman
       shell: bash
       run: |
+        set -euo pipefail
+        if [[ -n "${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT:-}" ]]; then
+          echo "Sandboxes run on the gateway at ${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT}; skipping rootless Podman setup."
+          exit 0
+        fi
         test -f /sys/fs/cgroup/cgroup.controllers || { echo "::error::cgroups v2 required"; exit 1; }
         whoami_user="$(whoami)"
         grep -q "^${whoami_user}:" /etc/subuid || sudo usermod --add-subuids 100000-165535 --add-subgids 100000-165535 "${whoami_user}"
@@ -380,6 +396,14 @@ runs:
     - name: Configure OpenShell gateway
       shell: bash
       run: |
+        set -euo pipefail
+        # This writes the configuration for a gateway running on this machine.
+        # An external gateway is configured where it runs, not here, and
+        # writing a local config would not reach it.
+        if [[ -n "${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT:-}" ]]; then
+          echo "Using the external gateway at ${OPENSHELL_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT}; skipping local gateway configuration."
+          exit 0
+        fi
         source "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/.github/scripts/openshell-version.sh"
         mkdir -p $HOME/.config/openshell/
         cat > $HOME/.config/openshell/gateway.env << EOF
@@ -395,11 +419,28 @@ runs:
 
     - name: Install OpenShell CLI
       shell: bash
-      run: "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/.github/scripts/install-openshell.sh"
+      run: |
+        set -euo pipefail
+        # The CLI is needed wherever the gateway runs. A runner image that
+        # already ships it does not need the installer, which requires sudo and
+        # reaches a CDN.
+        if command -v openshell >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+          echo "openshell is already installed: $(command -v openshell)"
+          exit 0
+        fi
+        "$GITHUB_ACTION_PATH/.github/scripts/install-openshell.sh"
 
     - name: Install validation dependencies
       shell: bash
-      run: pip install --quiet "jsonschema>=4.18.0"
+      run: |
+        set -euo pipefail
+        # Already satisfied on an image that ships it, and pip refuses to
+        # install into an externally managed environment without being told to.
+        if python3 -c "import jsonschema" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+          echo "jsonschema is already available"
+          exit 0
+        fi
+        pip install --quiet "jsonschema>=4.18.0"
 
     - name: Set up Go for target repo pre-commit hooks
       if: hashFiles(format('{0}/go.mod', inputs.target-repo)) != ''
